In article <19273@helios.TAMU.EDU> z0w3116@venus.tamu.edu writes:
>I have this my best ever character (-26 AC, +6 Excalibur) standing in front 
>of the castle. Now suppose I survived the castle level, is it worth to put
>on a helm of opposite alignment to my character Chaotic after going down
>to hell? I heard that only chaotic character can pray in hell.

If you aren't already Chaotic, go for it!

If you are, don't bother.  You have reached the portion of the game where
the only alignment to be is Chaotic.

DEFINITE SPOILERS BELOW


Take you helm of opposite alignment seriously-- uncurse it, enchant it, and
rustproof it.  You can now take advantage of the lawful AND chaotic
alignments with no detriment to your character whatsoever.

Become lawful to make holy water at will and to get Mjollnir.

Become chaotic if you prefer Stormbringer or if you need some unholy water.

Remain chaotic for hell so that you can pray.

If you are not chaotic when you get the amulet, there is a chance of going
DOWN dungeon levels when you used an UP staircase!  To counter this, just
use that helm to become chaotic.

What a bargain!  Of course if you started chaotic, the benefits reduce
somewhat, but it's still useful for Mjollnir and holy water.
